module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.sweep_terminated_by_process_death_rather_than_a_typed_refusal

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data sweep_terminated_by_process_death_rather_than_a_typed_refusal: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "sweep_terminated_by_process_death_rather_than_a_typed_refusal" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a corpus sweep ends by process death, so it reports less than it measured and looks like it stopped for a reason** (INVALID STATE: an instrument folds over a population one subject at a time, and the process is killed by the host -- SIGSEGV from unbounded native recursion in the interpreter -- partway through the fold. DESIGN section 5 admits two arms, succeed fully or fail with a typed located diagnostic, and this is neither: the run produces no cause, no locus and no count, because the code that would have produced them is not running any more. ",

    "HARM, AND IT IS THE SELF-CONCEALING KIND. Nothing can enroll the class, because there is no diagnostic to key on; nothing can attribute it, because there is no locus; and nothing can bound it, because there is no count of what was skipped. Worse than either, the survivors are indistinguishable from a complete answer at the only grain anyone reads: a sweep that died at the twentieth of five thousand subjects and a sweep that finished clean both present as a list of findings and an absence of alarms. Whoever reads it learns that no suspect was found, which is true, and infers that the population was examined, which is false. The exit status is the only channel carrying the difference, and it is the one channel a person reading a report does not see. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN (2026-09-06, complexity-lens lane): v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.corpus_census census_for_paths over a stratified sample of the tracked corpus dies with SIGSEGV around the twentieth subject, reproduced twice. The subject it dies ON analyses cleanly when handed to the same instrument alone, so the cause is accumulation across subjects within one process and not any one subject's shape -- which is what makes it a property of the SWEEP rather than of a datum, and therefore invisible to every per-subject control. ",

    "WHY IT IS NOT ONE OF THE ROWS BESIDE IT, checked at identity grain over gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster rather than by memory. ",

    "It is not `absorbing_fallback`: that class has a failure arm that WIDENS -- it computes a superset and calls it an answer, so the deficit is concealed by a value the program chose to produce. Here no arm executes at all. The two are opposite ends of the same obligation: an absorbing arm answers when it should refuse, and this one cannot reach the point of refusing. A repair for one does nothing for the other, because a typed cause added downstream of the death is never reached. ",

    "It is not `absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked`, which is the nearest and the tempting one. There the instrument RAN over its whole subject and the absence of a record is what carries no distinction. Here the instrument did not run over its whole subject, and the missing records were never attempted. That difference decides the repair: the other class is fixed by recording the looked-at set, and doing that here records a set that is itself truncated by the same defect -- the receipt would be short and would say so about nothing. ",

    "It is not `roster_is_its_own_denominator`: that class is a hand-authored list unjoined to any statement of what it should cover. This population IS derived -- corpus_gate discovers its subjects from the module index -- so the denominator is known and correct, and the defect is that the fold over it terminates early. A correct denominator makes this class MORE legible, not less: it is what would let a survivor count be compared against an expected one, which is the mitigation available before the wall lands. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder. This is not the bottom rung, it is silent wrongness, which DESIGN section 5 places outside the ladder and forbids outright -- a run that dies is consumed as a run that finished, and no modeled machinery contains the harm. Calling it mitigatable would be inflation: nothing today bounds, counts or types it. ",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed, and the reason it is not merely mitigatable is that the property is decidable rather than a fact about external reality. Native stack exhaustion in the interpreter is not an undecidable predicate about the analysed program; it is the absence of a bound on the interpreter's own recursion. A depth-bounded or explicitly-stacked walk converts an unbounded native recursion into a typed refusal that carries its locus and its depth, which is a wall available now with no missing grounding. It is not structurally impossible, because the walk depth remains representable -- the refusal is derived, not constructed away. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the interpreter's node walk carries an explicit stack or an explicit depth bound, so exceeding it raises a located typed diagnostic instead of terminating the process. It must be SUFFICIENT FOR the general case rather than for the specimen: any traversal deep enough to exhaust the native stack refuses with a cause and a locus, whichever entry point reached it -- not a per-instrument guard around census_for_paths, and not a larger stack, which moves the cliff without typing it. A batching driver for one sweep CONTRIBUTES to living with the class and does not retire it. ",

    "THE INTERIM MITIGATION IS BUILT, AND IT IS NOT THE CLIMB. Getting from OUTSIDE the ladder onto rung 1 is not the same move as climbing 1 to 2, and it is not optional: silent wrongness is forbidden outright, so a mitigation that ends the silence is owed as soon as the class is classified honestly -- an honest classification that changes nothing about what gets built is rung inflation wearing the opposite costume. v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.corpus_gate corpus_gate_disposition_over decides COVERAGE before any other arm: the discovered population and the reported rows are walked in lockstep and the first divergence ends the covered prefix, so a report that covers less than the population it names refuses with CorpusCoverageIncomplete carrying the missing subjects BY NAME. It is an identity join and not a count equality, which is the difference between catching a truncated sweep and catching only some of them: a batch re-run after a death reports the right NUMBER of rows over the wrong subjects. WHAT IT DOES NOT DO, CORRECTED HERE BECAUSE THIS ROW FIRST OVERSTATED IT AND A ROW ABOUT SILENT WRONGNESS MAY NOT CARRY AN INFLATED CLAIM. Review 61363 read the code rather than the sentence: corpus_gate evaluates corpus_rows_for_paths to completion BEFORE the join runs, so a SIGSEGV during collection kills the process with the join never reached. The mitigation therefore does NOT contain the in-process crash and never could from that position. What it converts is a REPORT SHORT OF ITS POPULATION -- rows assembled across batches after a death, a truncated row set arriving from anywhere -- from indistinguishable-from-clean into a typed refusal naming the missing subjects. The crash arm is untouched and stays below the ladder; the assembled-report arm is what reached rung 1. Containing the crash needs a SURVIVING REPORTING BOUNDARY: something outside the dying process that knows the population and observes the absence, which does not exist here and is not claimed. ",

    "ITS EVIDENCE DOES NOT RETIRE ON THE CLIMB. Three witnesses in v2.test.claim.complexity.accumulator_copy_corpus_path_test execute on every push: a truncated report refuses, a right-sized report over the wrong subjects refuses, a report carrying subjects the population does not contain refuses, an empty population with a reported row refuses rather than reading clean, and a complete report over the same population reaches its ordinary verdict -- the positive control without which a guard that refused everything would satisfy every red beside it. The surplus half and the empty-population case were found by review 61363, not by the author: the walk checked only that DISCOVERED ran out, so leftover rows were accepted, and the degenerate shape let the population floor count reported rows instead of the discovered population -- the floor's own red control defeated by the guard that runs before it. Verified discriminating by mutation rather than by reading: neutering the join to answer 'nothing missing' turns both reds red and leaves the control green. When the depth-bounded walk lands, these stay enrolled as the regression control that the higher rung is real. ",

    "A NEIGHBOUR THAT LOOKS LIKE THIS CLASS AND IS ITS OPPOSITE, recorded because the confusion is available to anyone reading a floor log and was made once already. The required floor reports interrupted_before_verdict when a witness crosses the CPU deadline v2.workflow.required_floor required_floor_claim_cpu_safety_limit_ms declares -- named rather than transcribed, because that module's own prose carries a stale ten-fold figure for it in nine places -- and 'the run stopped partway and the identity has no verdict' is superficially this row's sentence. It is not this class and the population does not widen to cover it. The floor's preemption is a TYPED, LOCATED, COUNTED refusal -- raised_by=cpu_deadline, the measured CPU against the declared line, the identity named, the totals carried as interrupted_cpu_deadline and interrupted_wall_deadline, and the lane BLOCKS on it -- which is precisely the arm DESIGN section 5 asks for and precisely what this class lacks. The distinguishing question is not whether a run ended early; it is whether ending early produced a cause, a locus and a count, or produced silence that reads as completion. A budget preemption is the floor working; a SIGSEGV is the floor having nothing to work with. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when an instrument folds over a population in one process, ask what its output looks like if the process dies at subject k. If the answer is 'the same shape as a complete run, one page shorter', the sweep has no completion channel and its report is an unstated assumption about its own exit status.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
